eference standard result was conducted without knowledge of the index test results. In the “Flow and Timing” domain, 11 out pf 16 studies were rated as low risk and 5 out of 16 studies were rated as unclear risk due to they did not mention the time interval between the index test and the reference standard. Fig. 2 Quality assessment of included studies according to QUADAS-AI Pooled performance of AI algorithms Our meta-analysis indicated that these AI models exhibit high classification accuracy for benign and malignant breast tumors. The pooled sensitivity was 0.90 (95% CI: 0.85–0.94) and specificity was 0.88 (0.81–0.93), achieving an AUC of 0.95 (0.93–0.97) for all AI algorithms (See Fig. 3 for details). The τ 2 of sensitivity and specificity were 0.66 (0.21–2.12) and 0.91(0.38–2.20), respectively. The PLR was 7.5(4.7–11.9), the NLR was 0.11 (0.07–0.18) and the DOR was 67(33–137). In the results given by the HSROC model (See Fig. 4 for details), the threshold (beta) was 0.16 (−0.57–0.89), and the Z statistic was 0.42, with a corresponding \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
